    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Fixes infinite generation loop (token 197 / tab) when a tool has `strict: true` and empty parameters (`{\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}, \"required\": []}`)\n- The xgrammar grammar for such schemas only accepts whitespace, causing the model to generate tabs forever\n- Both the xgrammar-builtin path (`_dump_tool_for_xgrammar`) and the vLLM-defined structural tag path (`get_function_parameters`) now treat empty-properties schemas as unconstrained, since the only valid output is `{}`\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Verify with Qwen 3.x model and a tool with empty properties and `strict: true`\n- [ ] Verify that tools with non-empty properties and `strict: true` still work correctly\n- [ ] Verify that `strict: false` tools are unaffected\n\n## Notes\n\n- No duplicate PR exists for this issue\n- AI assistance was used in developing this fix\n- This fix affects `structural_tag_registry.py` only — the grammar/structural tag layer that every parser needs, per the AGENTS.md guideline\n\nFixes https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/50989\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
